// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 05-value-object-semantics
// facility: rule.value-object.binding-form [Binding-Form-Redeclared] (a `for` header governs its body); D-0131; conf.redeclared-for-variable-rejected
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.duplicate-local (static)
//
// The variable a `for` header declares belongs to the body's region: the
// body may not declare it again (a block nested in the body may).

import std;

fn main()
{
    for (i32 i = 0; i < 3; i += 1)
    {
        i32 i = 5;
        printf("%v\n", i);
    }
}
